			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-1630434">
									

<p>That's a cultural difference thing. &quot;Carers&quot; is not a term used in America. &quot;Parent or gaurdian&quot; is the usual phrasing. Sometimes the term &quot;caregiver&quot; is used, but that more often refers to a nurse or other professional being paid for their services.</p>
<p>And &quot;caretaker&quot; is someone paid to maintain a building or property, it is never used to refer to someone taking care of people.</p>

